Module panel-findings-store.

REALIZES (L2, source semantics):
- sr:L2:S-S4: Seam S-S4 — panel / attack → findings store
  [a:S-S4:seam] Seam S-S4 has producer panel / attack and consumer findings store; its contract is the Finding record; its crossing example is the literal {"id": "F-017", "source": "stub-builder", "severity": "critical", "clause": "spec.md:§3/C2", "text": "signature satisfiable by empty redirect", "replay": "attacks/stub-017/"}; status filled.
    grounded (primary) in sf:f743e46fcb17bf1038e2560e, line 119: | S-S4 | panel / attack → findings store | Finding record | `{"id": "F-017", "source": "stub-builder", "severity": "critical", "clause": "spec.md:§3/C2", "text": "signature satisfiable by empty redirect", "replay": "attacks/stub-017/"}` | filled |
- sr:L2:Finding: Finding record
  [a:Finding:record] Finding is an event record and is append-only.
    grounded (primary) in sf:bbdecf529e21b598e5c59b46, line 85: Records: `Spec {path, rev}` (state) · `GradeRecord` (event, per W-CS2-N) · `Finding` (event, append-only) · `Disposition {finding_id, kind ∈ resolved | otherwise | deferred | rejected, reasons}` (event) · `WalkItem {citer, cites, status}` (state, derived) · `LedgerEntry` (event, hash-chained) · `ClosureRow {clause, class, falsifier, validation, gate}` (derived, C-S1 only).
    grounded (context) in sf:590259498f7dac6171526d27, line 127: - **V-S1 — Findings and ledger immutability.** Scope: every commit in the repository history, over `findings/**` and `ledger/**`. Generator: n ≥ 100 pipeline runs plus seeded tamper attempts. Property: every commit's diff over those paths is append-only — no modification, no deletion. Pinned witnesses: W-CS4-N (append), W-CS7-Δ1 (blocked rewrite).
  [a:Finding:fields] A Finding record carries the fields id (of the form F-<n>), source, severity, clause, text, and replay; the source states this shape only by literal example — the S-S4 crossing example and W-CS4-N — and replay appears in one of the two examples.
    grounded (primary) in sf:f743e46fcb17bf1038e2560e, line 119: | S-S4 | panel / attack → findings store | Finding record | `{"id": "F-017", "source": "stub-builder", "severity": "critical", "clause": "spec.md:§3/C2", "text": "signature satisfiable by empty redirect", "replay": "attacks/stub-017/"}` | filled |
    grounded (primary) in sf:3482babe3032ab57d14942de, line 56: - **W-CS4-N (nominal):** closure-auditor perspective on a fixture with an unwitnessed rule → appends `findings/cycle-1/closure-auditor-001.json` = `{"id": "F-<n>", "source": "closure-auditor", "severity": "major", "clause": "spec.md:§4/R-2", "text": "R-2 names no witness; pairing is unidirectional"}`; property: **all pre-existing files under `findings/` byte-identical** — append-only, the absence of modification is the assertion.

CLOSURES (L3, ratified design; not source semantics):
  [c:store:FindingInput] {"definition":"Omit<Finding, 'id'>","note":"the store assigns id","type":"FindingInput"}
  [c:store:appendFinding] {"export":"appendFinding","signature":"appendFinding(rootDir: string, cycle: number, input: FindingInput): Finding"}
  [c:store:component] {"component":"panel-findings-store","responsibility":"append-only persistence of Finding records; owns the findings/ tree and nothing else (no dispositions, no walk items, no ledger)"}
  [c:store:errors] {"classes":["FindingValidationError","FindingWriteConflictError","FindingStoreCorruptionError"],"extend":"Error"}
  [c:store:getFinding] {"export":"getFinding","signature":"getFinding(rootDir: string, id: string): Finding | undefined"}
  [c:store:listFindings] {"export":"listFindings","order":"ascending by numeric id","signature":"listFindings(rootDir: string, cycle?: number): Finding[]"}
  [c:store:no-mutation-api] {"rule":"the public API has no update, delete or rename function; the omission is the mechanical guarantee of append-only at the API surface"}
  [c:store:on-disk-layout] {"path":"${rootDir}/findings/cycle-${cycle}/${source}-${seq3}.json","seq3":"3-digit zero-padded, 1-based, scoped to (cycle, source)"}
